" /></p>","subject":"TEST ID-25 [ DIGITAL LOGIC-3] - 2026"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/657b638b-838d-411b-a942-bd623362933c.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/2347aad0-3474-4459-bd4d-f3492d63b355.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"TEST ID-25 [ DIGITAL LOGIC-3] - 2026"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/b4840d7b-e5fc-4c29-acdc-530c2f1d3ff7.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/57c4fa67-c4e0-4af2-a390-d9540af2fc7f.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"TEST ID-25 [ DIGITAL LOGIC-3] - 2026"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"24","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/020b9eb6-09b0-4d23-801e-d7daba053d0b.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-wl-assets.classplus.co/production/single/vlvkc/04254bd5-3730-4db2-9fba-adc9289f1cf9.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"24","high":"24"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/3a9b7861-5999-48a1-ba37-a0accf517f36.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<span>Step 1: Understanding the Structure<o:p></o:p></span>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>The <strong>64 bits</strong> are divided into <strong>16 groups of 4 bits each</strong> (since 64/4 = 16).<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><strong><span>First Level:</span></strong><span> Each group of 4 bits uses a 4-bit CLA. This quickly computes the sum and carry-out for each group.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><strong><span>Second Level:</span></strong><span> The 16 group carry-outs are combined using another level of carry look-ahead logic to compute the final carries.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<span>Step 2: Calculating the Delay<o:p></o:p></span>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><strong><span>The delay in a multi-level CLA adder</span></strong><span> depends on the logic required to generate all the necessary carry signals.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>The delay formula for a <strong>two-level CLA using k-bit modules</strong> to add n bits is:<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><strong><span>T_CLA = (6 + 2 &times; ceil(log</span>ₖ</strong><strong><span> n)) </span></strong><strong><span>&times;</span></strong> <strong><span>&delta;</span></strong><o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>Where:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><span>o<span> </span></span><code><span>k</span></code><span> = size of each CLA module = 4<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>o<span> </span></span><code><span>n</span></code><span> = total number of bits = 64<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>o<span> </span></span><code><span>&delta;</span></code><span> = delay of a basic gate = 2 ns<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<span>Step-by-Step Delay Calculation:<o:p></o:p></span>\n<p><span><span>1.<span> </span></span><strong><span>Calculate log</span>ₖ</strong><strong><span> n:</span></strong><span><br />log</span>₄<span> 64 = log</span>₂<span> 64 / log</span>₂<span> 4 = 6 / 2 = 3<br />So, ceil(log</span>₄<span> 64) = 3<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>2.<span> </span></span><strong><span>Plug into the formula:</span></strong><span><br />T_CLA = 6 + 2 &times; 3 = 6 + 6 = 12<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>3.<span> </span></span><strong><span>Multiply by basic gate delay:</span></strong><span><br />Total delay = 12 &times; 2 ns = <strong>24 ns</strong><o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<span>Step 3: Interpreting Each Term in Formula<o:p></o:p></span>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>The <strong>6</strong> in the formula accounts for the internal delays of the CLA logic for generate/propagate and the final sum calculation.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>The <strong>2 &times; ceil(log₄</strong><strong> 64)</strong> comes from the hierarchical combination of CLA modules. Since each higher level combines the carry outputs of lower modules, this adds more delay as the number of modules increases.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span> The <strong>&delta;</strong> is just the basic gate delay.<br /><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/526e38c0-59a0-49dd-b0c7-9d2472f0b856.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></span></p>","subject":"TEST ID-25 [ DIGITAL LOGIC-3] - 2026"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/cb139eb5-b7dd-4aac-a2d8-d753aae19dc5.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/8318dd79-50a7-4e59-80ef-4bc1089f8341.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/fcec4c52-2d4c-44ea-902d-69f3bee5fe3e.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p></p>","subject":"TEST ID-25 [ DIGITAL LOGIC-3] 